      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Expressed as a mixed number in its lowest terms, $6\\times \\frac{5}{7}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 5}{7}=\\frac{30}{7}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{30}{7}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n30÷7=4\\,\\text{R}\\,2=4\\,\\frac{2}{7}\n$$",
